# Defensive ignore list only.
#
# package.json declares a "files" allowlist (index.mjs, lib, vendor, assets,
# locale, cordis.patch.yml, README.md, README.en.md, LICENSE), and npm treats
# that allowlist as authoritative: with "files" present this file has NO effect
# on the tarball. Verified empirically in this repo:
#   - `npm pack --dry-run --json` lists the same 29 entries with and without
#     this file, even when it contains `lib/` and `assets/` (which stayed in).
#   - A decoy root file absent from "files" is excluded either way; the same
#     decoy IS packed once "files" is removed, and IS excluded again by this
#     file in that situation.
# So the real protection is "files"; these rules are a safety net that only
# takes effect if the "files" allowlist is ever removed.
#
# Rules mirror .gitignore, applied to the publish payload instead of git.
.github/
.vscode/
state/
tmp/
test/
scripts/
docs/
coverage/

# Never publish credentials or local env files.
.env*
.npmrc

# Packaging leftovers and generated logs.
*.tgz
*.log

# Runtime/editor cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
